From: Michiel <367462+meghuizen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:29:23 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/3] selftests: build and run the openat2 tests again

tools/testing/selftests/Makefile lists "openat2" in TARGETS, but the
tests now live in filesystems/openat2 and there is no openat2 directory
any more. filesystems/openat2 is not in TARGETS and filesystems/Makefile
does not descend into it, so openat2_test, resolve_test,
rename_attack_test and emptypath_test are not built or run by
"make kselftest", and "make TARGETS=openat2" fails with "No targets
specified and no makefile found".

Replace the stale entry with filesystems/openat2, next to the other
filesystems/ targets.

Tested on x86-64: "make -C tools/testing/selftests
TARGETS=filesystems/openat2 all" builds all four programs, and they run
(on a 6.18 host kernel, which lacks O_REGULAR and O_EMPTYPATH, the two
subtests for those flags fail and the rest pass).

Assisted-by: Claude
---
Impact: low -- test coverage: the openat2 tests are not built by
"make kselftest" without this.

Independent of the rest of the series; it can go to linux-kselftest on
its own. No Fixes: tag: the commit that moved the tests is not in the
history available here.

 tools/testing/selftests/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/testing/selftests/Makefile b/tools/testing/selftests/Makefile
index 2d960626750e..d6ed25cbf7f7 100644
--- a/tools/testing/selftests/Makefile
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/Makefile
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ TARGETS += filesystems/binderfs
 TARGETS += filesystems/epoll
 TARGETS += filesystems/failfs
 TARGETS += filesystems/fat
+TARGETS += filesystems/openat2
 TARGETS += filesystems/overlayfs
 TARGETS += filesystems/statmount
 TARGETS += filesystems/mount-notify
@@ -103,7 +104,6 @@ TARGETS += prctl
 TARGETS += proc
 TARGETS += pstore
 TARGETS += ptrace
-TARGETS += openat2
 TARGETS += rdma
 TARGETS += resctrl
 TARGETS += riscv
